    },
    {
      "line": 981,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The pain wasn’t fury; it was the weight of an unhealed wound, the burden of absorbing the final, agonized thoughts of billions."
    },
    {
      "line": 982,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt stood within the crater of his own history, the dragon armor humming a low counterpoint to the desert’s lament."
    },
    {
      "line": 983,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He hadn’t silenced the Heart; he’d finally allowed it to be heard."
    },
    {
      "line": 984,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 985,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The tendrils slowly retracted, sinking back into the fused glass like weary mourners returning to a grave."
    },
    {
      "line": 986,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The obsidian plain settled, the violent heaving ceasing."
    },
    {
      "line": 987,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Where they retreated, the sickly green veins dimmed, replaced by a faint, steady silver luminescence – the Heart’s own essence, cleansed, however briefly, of the corrupted grief.",
      "inferred": {
        "action": [
          {
            "label": "retreat",
            "confidence": 0.9
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 988,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A profound silence fell, deeper and older than before, filled not with rage, but with a weary, ancient sorrow."
    },
    {
      "line": 989,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The applicator’s warning flickered out."
    },
    {
      "line": 990,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The armor’s empathetic glow faded, leaving Geralt standing alone in the glassy scar, the weight of three thousand years pressing down with a crushing, quiet understanding."
    },
    {
      "line": 991,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "This was the price."
    },
    {
      "line": 992,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "This silence was the echo of his victory."
    },
    {
      "line": 993,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He turned north, towards the chasm’s edge, the Star Needle’s pull guiding him away from the Heart’s wounded memory."
    },
    {
      "line": 994,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He walked lighter, not from absolution, but from shared burden."
    },
    {
      "line": 995,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The desert watched him go, its gaze still heavy, but no longer holding him at bay."
    },
